WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.722
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:06.022 --> 00:00:09.431
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.731 --> 00:00:16.029
Unit two: Inversion for Emphasis. Today you will invert subject and verb after negative adverbials.

4
00:00:16.329 --> 00:00:18.947
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.028
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.883 --> 00:00:25.140
Never have I.

7
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.846
Never have I means an inverted opening with never.

8
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.345
Never have I seen such a view.

9
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.591
Your turn. Say: Never have I.

10
00:00:37.433 --> 00:00:38.760
Never have I.

11
00:00:39.517 --> 00:00:40.878
Rarely does.

12
00:00:41.883 --> 00:00:44.696
Rarely does means an inverted opening with rarely.

13
00:00:45.283 --> 00:00:46.911
Rarely does he complain.

14
00:00:47.517 --> 00:00:50.471
Your turn. Say: Rarely does.

15
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:54.625
Rarely does.

16
00:00:55.383 --> 00:00:56.419
Not only.

17
00:00:57.417 --> 00:01:00.299
Not only means an inverted opening that adds a point.

18
00:01:00.883 --> 00:01:03.254
Not only did she win, she broke a record.

19
00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:06.572
Your turn. Say: Not only.

20
00:01:09.433 --> 00:01:10.365
Not only.

21
00:01:11.117 --> 00:01:12.060
Seldom.

22
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.433
Seldom means not often, in formal writing.

23
00:01:16.017 --> 00:01:17.552
Seldom have we met.

24
00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.802
Your turn. Say: Seldom.

25
00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:24.563
Seldom.

26
00:01:25.317 --> 00:01:26.353
Emphatic.

27
00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.640
Emphatic means strongly expressed.

28
00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:31.855
An emphatic statement.

29
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.009
Your turn. Say: Emphatic.

30
00:01:37.867 --> 00:01:38.647
Emphatic.

31
00:01:39.383 --> 00:01:40.570
Formal register.

32
00:01:41.583 --> 00:01:44.721
Formal register means a serious style of language.

33
00:01:45.317 --> 00:01:47.665
Inversion suits formal register.

34
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:51.483
Your turn. Say: Formal register.

35
00:01:54.333 --> 00:01:55.636
Formal register.

36
00:01:56.383 --> 00:01:57.164
Fronting.

37
00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.544
Fronting means moving a word to the start.

38
00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:02.801
Fronting adds emphasis.

39
00:02:03.417 --> 00:02:06.208
Your turn. Say: Fronting.

40
00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:09.986
Fronting.

41
00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.053
Literary style.

42
00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:16.083
Literary style means the style of books and poems.

43
00:02:16.683 --> 00:02:18.021
A literary style.

44
00:02:18.617 --> 00:02:21.594
Your turn. Say: Literary style.

45
00:02:24.433 --> 00:02:25.968
Literary style.

46
00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:30.673
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:37.255
Visal, which is stronger: I have never seen such a view, or Never have I seen such a view?

48
00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:47.655
The second. When a negative adverbial begins the sentence, the subject and auxiliary swap places: Never have I seen such a view.

49
00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.239
Which words trigger it?

50
00:02:51.350 --> 00:03:04.416
Never, rarely, seldom, hardly, no sooner, not only, under no circumstances. If there is no auxiliary, add do, does or did: Rarely does he complain.

51
00:03:05.517 --> 00:03:06.564
Is it common?

52
00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:19.579
It belongs to formal speech, speeches and literary writing. In casual talk it sounds theatrical, so use it for effect and not in every paragraph.

53
00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.663
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:23.517 --> 00:03:29.615
Grammar focus: Inversion: negative adverbial plus auxiliary plus subject plus verb.

55
00:03:29.915 --> 00:03:31.020
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:31.717 --> 00:03:34.564
Never have I seen such a beautiful view.

57
00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.856
Rarely does he complain about his work.

58
00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.818
Not only did she win, she also broke the record.

59
00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:49.111
After a negative adverbial at the start, put the auxiliary before the subject. Add do / does / did if there is none.

60
00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:53.129
Be careful! Don't say: Never I have seen it.

61
00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:57.252
Say: Never have I seen it.

62
00:03:57.552 --> 00:03:58.983
Invert after never.

63
00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:02.663
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:04.746
A Rare Talent.

65
00:04:05.046 --> 00:04:09.066
Rarely does a student combine talent with such discipline.

66
00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:13.041
Never have I seen anyone practise so patiently.

67
00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:17.647
Not only did she win the prize, she also helped the others.

68
00:04:18.633 --> 00:04:20.819
Seldom has the school been so proud.

69
00:04:21.833 --> 00:04:25.029
Inversion makes these sentences sound formal and dramatic.

70
00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:30.100
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:33.054
Never blank such a beautiful view.

72
00:04:33.354 --> 00:04:37.031
A, I have seen. B, have I seen. C, I saw.

73
00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.508
The answer is B: have I seen.

74
00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.313
Rarely blank he complain.

75
00:04:45.613 --> 00:04:48.837
A, does. B, do. C, did he.

76
00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.458
The answer is A: does.

77
00:04:55.617 --> 00:04:56.827
Which is correct?

78
00:04:57.127 --> 00:05:02.336
A, Not only she won.. B, Not only did she win.. C, Not only she did win..

79
00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.643
The answer is B: Not only did she win..

80
00:05:09.783 --> 00:05:12.514
Inversion is mostly used in blank English.

81
00:05:12.814 --> 00:05:16.630
A, formal. B, text-message. C, baby.

82
00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:21.899
The answer is A: formal.

83
00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:25.746
According to the reading, what did she help?

84
00:05:26.046 --> 00:05:29.572
A, the others. B, the teacher. C, the judges.

85
00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:35.261
The answer is A: the others.

86
00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:39.653
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:40.517 --> 00:05:44.432
Try rewriting a sentence using inversion, starting with 'Never have I...'

88
00:05:53.217 --> 00:05:54.624
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:54.924 --> 00:06:05.822
Never have I felt so proud of my class. Never have I seen students work so hard together. I use inversion to make my feelings sound strong and formal.

90
00:06:06.122 --> 00:06:07.739
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:15.575
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and inversion: negative adverbial plus auxiliary plus subject plus verb.

92
00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:19.944
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

93
00:06:20.244 --> 00:06:22.675
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

94
00:06:22.975 --> 00:06:26.220
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

